(768, '2', 'Are there CAPM online courses available for working professionals?', '<p>Yes, many online CAPM courses are designed for working professionals. These courses offer flexible schedules, including self-paced learning and live weekend or evening sessions. They follow PMI guidelines and provide the required 23 hours of project management education, helping learners balance work and study.</p>', '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
(769, '2', 'What’s next after completing the CAPM certification course — should I go for PMP?', '<p>After completing the CAPM certification course, pursuing the PMP certification is recommended once you gain the required project management experience. PMP is suited for professionals managing more complex projects and offers advanced knowledge and better career prospects.</p>', '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
(770, '2', 'What does CAPM stand for?', '<p>CAPM stands for Certified Associate in Project Management. In project management, CAPM validates foundational knowledge and skills in project management practices and methodologies.</p>', '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
(771, '2', 'What is the difference between CAPM® & PMP®?', '<p>The main difference between CAPM® (Certified Associate in Project Management) and PMP® (Project Management Professional) lies in their target audience and level of expertise. CAPM® is designed for entry-level project managers or those with limited experience, focusing on basic project management concepts. PMP®, offered by&nbsp;the Project Management Institute,&nbsp;on the other hand, is for experienced professionals, requiring a deeper understanding of advanced project management techniques and leadership skills. PMP® certification generally holds more value in the industry due to its higher level of difficulty and experience prerequisites.</p>', '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
(772, '2', 'How many questions are there in the CAPM® certification exam?', '<p>The CAPM® certification exam&nbsp;covers 150 questions, out of which 15 questions are considered as pre-test questions used for future tests and are not scored. You will not be communicated about these questions; they are randomly chosen. Therefore, you should answer all 150 questions with the same seriousness.</p>', '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
(773, '2', 'What\'s next after CAPM® Certification?', '<p>After completing the CAPM®&nbsp;certification&nbsp;training&nbsp;program, you can take the PMP® certification training, Digital Project Manager, or PMP® Plus program. At the next level, you have Prince2® certification training, MSP® Foundation and Practitioner, Prince2® Agile Foundation and Practitioner and best of all, you can get the Project Management Certification (PGP in Project Management) program.</p>', '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
(774, '2', 'Is the CAPM® course difficult to learn?', NULL, '2025-09-07 23:53:15', '2025-09-07 23:52:14', '2025-09-07 23:53:15'),
